  "title": "The kinds of place, organization, person, facility, event, service and topic, and what apps call them",
  "notes": [
    "Every app uses these names for a kind, so a district is a District and a community is a Communities group everywhere.",
    "singular names one of the kind (a Type row, a card). plural names the group or heading.",
    "facet is the schema type a kind belongs to, and facets lists them in the order filters show them. A filter is named for its facet (Place, Organization, Person), not for the app's own word.",
    "A Place is a territory: a district, a city or town, a community, an area, a region, or the county. A Facility is a building or site, shown beside Places. An Event is a gathering.",
    "An Area is a named neighborhood, valley or part of a city that is not a city, town or community of its own. A Region is a larger part of the county that holds several communities.",
    "An organization kind is the organizationClassification of its record (department, division, court ...). association is for organizations that are not government."
  ],
